<mjml lang="en">
  <mj-head>
    <!--
      PROBE — the head-resident mode-fork swap (2026-08-24).

      Not a catalog page. Build, send dist/probe_head-resident-swap_live.html
      through EN to EoA, and read the LIGHT/DARK PAIRS of each client — this
      probe is entirely about mode forking, so every verdict needs both halves.

      WHAT MOVED, AND WHY THIS SEND EXISTS. The light/dark SWAP mechanism
      (.dark-only plain hide, :root color-scheme, the [data-ogsc] and
      prefers-color-scheme reveal pairs) now lives in the page-template head
      behind data-en-tools-template-css, so an email built WITHOUT the
      Template Styles block no longer shows every twin twice. The dark
      REPAINTS stayed in styles.css. Browser-verified already: with the sheet
      stripped, exactly one twin set per mode. What a browser CANNOT verify is
      EN's send pipeline, which is what the S series measures.

      THE ONE HAZARD: same-condition @media folding. EN folds every
      same-condition block into the FIRST occurrence's position (measured
      2026-08-19). The head now carries @media blocks for the ogsc 9999px and
      prefers-color-scheme conditions holding ONLY the swap; styles.css's
      blocks with those conditions hold the repaints. At send the repaints
      should fold up AFTER the head's swap rules — which is exactly today's
      in-block order — but "should" is the word this probe deletes.

      THIS PROBE CARRIES NO styles.css. Its body carries a small <style>
      mimicking the styles block's dark REPAINT blocks (same condition
      strings), so the fold happens exactly as it does for a real email.

        S1  Light-mode clients: exactly ONE of each labelled twin pair
            visible, the LIGHT one (Sun bar). Two bars of one pair = the swap
            failed; the pre-move failure mode was every twin doubled.
        S2  Dark-mode clients (applemail16_dm, iphone/android _dm,
            outlookcom-dm, gmailcom-dm): the DARK twin (Fern bar) only — AND
            the repaint fires: the "REPAINT CANARY" band must be Earth
            #362229 in dark mode, proving the body-carried repaint block
            still applies after folding against the head's swap block.
        S3  Outlook 2021 (Word): conditionals hide the dark twin from Word
            entirely, so the light bar alone, both modes. Word ignores
            @media, which is why the dark twin sits in a revealed
            conditional.
        S4  DELIVERED HTML (/app/acidtest/display/email_html/<TEST_ID>):
            (a) the .dark-only element carries an inlined display:none —
            EN inlining the head's plain hide, same as the mobile fork's
            (T1, measured 2026-08-24); (b) find both 9999px blocks and both
            prefers-color-scheme blocks in the delivered head and confirm
            the SWAP rules precede the REPAINT rules after folding.
        S5  The overlay heading ("OVERLAY CHECK") renders WHITE over the
            photo in every client — .overlay now serves from the head.
        S6  Regression: the viewport fork still forks (mobile bar under
            600px only), since this element also carries it.

      Colours are brand palette only (CLAUDE.md → Instrument colors):
      Sun #F7931E = light twin, Fern #39B54A = dark twin, Sky #5DD8D8 =
      structure, Earth #362229 = the repaint target.
    -->
    <mj-breakpoint width="600px" />
    <mj-title>PROBE — head-resident swap</mj-title>
    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-text color="#362229" font-size="16px" font-family="Tahoma, sans-serif" line-height="22px" css-class="wysiwyg" />
      <mj-image padding="0" />
    </mj-attributes>

    <!-- The head-resident element under test — byte-identical rules to
         main.mjml's, minus the label comments. -->
    <mj-raw>
      <style type="text/css" data-en-tools-template-css>
        .wysiwyg div *:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
        .wysiwyg div *:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
        .overlay h1, .overlay h2, .overlay h3, .overlay h4, .overlay h5,
        .overlay h6, .overlay span, .overlay p, .overlay a { color: #ffffff; }
        .mobile-only { display: none; }
        .dark-only { display: none; }
        :root { color-scheme: light dark; supported-color-schemes: light dark; }
        @media (max-width: 9998px) {
          .mobile-only { display: none !important; }
        }
        @media (max-width: 599px) {
          .desktop-only { display: none !important; }
          .mobile-only { display: block !important; }
        }
        @media only screen and (max-width: 9999px) {
          [data-ogsc] .dark-only { display: block !important; }
          [data-ogsc] .light-only { display: none !important; }
        }
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
          .light-only { display: none !important; }
          .dark-only { display: block !important; }
        }
      </style>
    </mj-raw>
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body background-color="#ffffff">

    <mj-section background-color="#362229" padding="12px 16px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text color="#8CC63F" align="center" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:3px;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;">S — HEAD-RESIDENT MODE-FORK SWAP · NO styles.css IN THIS EMAIL</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- The body-carried repaint mimic: same condition STRINGS as styles.css,
         repaints only — this is what must fold cleanly behind the head swap. -->
    <mj-raw>
      <style type="text/css">
        @media only screen and (max-width: 9999px) {
          [data-ogsc] .repaint-canary td { background-color: #362229 !important; }
          [data-ogsc] .repaint-canary p { color: #ffffff !important; }
        }
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
          .repaint-canary td { background-color: #362229 !important; }
          .repaint-canary p { color: #ffffff !important; }
        }
      </style>
    </mj-raw>

    <!-- S1/S2/S3 — a labelled twin pair, the exact light/dark idiom every
         image-bearing block uses. -->
    <mj-section background-color="#F5FAF1" padding="8px 16px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text padding="0"><p><b>TWIN PAIR</b> — exactly ONE bar below may be visible per client/mode. Sun = light twin, Fern = dark twin. Both visible = the swap failed (the pre-move defect).</p></mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-section background-color="#F7931E" padding="14px 16px" css-class="light-only">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0"><p style="font-weight:700;">LIGHT TWIN — correct in light mode and in all of Outlook desktop</p></mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-raw><!--[if !mso]><!--></mj-raw>
    <mj-section background-color="#39B54A" padding="14px 16px" css-class="dark-only">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0"><p style="font-weight:700;">DARK TWIN — correct in dark mode only; hidden from Word by the conditional</p></mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-raw><!--<![endif]--></mj-raw>

    <!-- S2 — does the body-carried repaint still fire after folding? -->
    <mj-section background-color="#F5FAF1" padding="8px 16px" css-class="repaint-canary">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0"><p><b>REPAINT CANARY</b> — Snow ground in light mode; must repaint to Earth (#362229) with white copy in dark mode. Still Snow in dark = the fold dropped the body repaints.</p></mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- S5 — .overlay served from the head -->
    <mj-section background-url="assets/photo-forest.jpg" background-size="cover" background-repeat="no-repeat" background-position="center center" padding="32px 0 32px">
      <mj-group>
        <mj-column width="25px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
        <mj-column width="550px">
          <mj-text css-class="overlay" padding="0"><h2 style="text-align:center;">OVERLAY CHECK — this heading must be WHITE in every client</h2></mj-text>
        </mj-column>
        <mj-column width="25px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
      </mj-group>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- S6 — viewport-fork regression -->
    <mj-section css-class="desktop-only" background-color="#006837" padding="12px 16px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text color="#ffffff" align="center" padding="0"><p style="font-weight:700;">S6 — DESKTOP BAR (viewport fork regression)</p></mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-raw><!--[if !mso]><!--></mj-raw>
    <mj-section css-class="mobile-only" background-color="#5DD8D8" padding="12px 16px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0"><p style="font-weight:700;">S6 — MOBILE BAR (under 600px only)</p></mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <mj-raw><!--<![endif]--></mj-raw>

    <mj-section background-color="#F5FAF1" padding="8px 16px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text padding="0"><p>S4 is read from the DELIVERED HTML: (a) inlined display:none on the .dark-only element; (b) after EN's same-condition fold, the swap rules must PRECEDE the repaint rules inside both merged dark blocks.</p></mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

  </mj-body>
</mjml>
